Title:
RemotePatcher

Type:
GitHub Tool

Short Summary (4-8 sentences max):
RemotePatcher is a small C++ utility that patches AMSI and ETW in a remote Windows process to reduce script/content scanning (AMSI) and telemetry generation (ETW). It performs remote memory patching using direct system calls generated via SysWhispers3, aiming to bypass user-mode API hooks commonly used by EDR. The repo includes an AMSI patch variant that returns an AMSI_RESULT_CLEAN-equivalent value using simple arithmetic instead of the common immediate constant pattern. It supports patching an existing PID or spawning a new process and patching it, with options to target AmsiScanBuffer vs AmsiOpenSession and to force-load amsi.dll. This is primarily useful for red teamers and pentesters experimenting with in-memory evasion and syscall-based tradecraft.

Technical Focus:
- Remote process memory patching (AMSI/ETW)
- Direct syscalls via SysWhispers3 (Nt* invocation)
- AMSI bypass targets (AmsiScanBuffer, AmsiOpenSession)
- ETW patching to suppress event emission
- EDR user-mode hook evasion concepts

Use Cases:
- Patch AMSI/ETW in a running offensive tooling host process (e.g., PowerShell, custom loaders)
- Spawn-and-patch a sacrificial process before executing .NET or script-based payloads
- Tradecraft experimentation with direct syscalls vs Win32 API calls under EDR
- Testing defensive detections for remote patching and AMSI/ETW tampering

Keywords:
AMSI, ETW, AmsiScanBuffer, AmsiOpenSession, amsi.dll, remote patching, process injection, WriteProcessMemory, direct syscall, SysWhispers3, NtWriteVirtualMemory, NtProtectVirtualMemory, EDR evasion, user-mode hooks, Windows internals, telemetry suppression, in-memory patch, C++ tool